unit":"source-explicit-context-tone-membership","tradition":"Chinese","witnessId":"HouHanShu91-JingFang","position":{"generation":null,"sequence":null,"cyclicCoordinate":null,"orientation":null},"sourceRefs":["chinese-expanded:houhan91"],"assertionLayer":"source-assertion","exceptions":[],"nativeRole":"徵","evidence":{"sourceId":"chinese-expanded:houhan91","normalizedTextPath":"state/research/chinese-expanded/houhan91.normalized.txt","startCodePoint":10753,"endCodePointExclusive":10812,"text":"遲時，八萬九千五百九十五。上生制時。遲時為宮，少出商，制時徵。 六日律，四寸五分小分五強。準，四尺五寸萬二百一十五。 "}},{"id":"chinese-expanded:lam:modes","nativeName":"Lam2024：六十調 as modal-final contexts","aliases":[],"unit":"source-qualified-pentatonic-mode-family","tradition":"Chinese","witnessId":"Lam2024","position":{"generation":null,"sequence":null,"cyclicCoordinate":null,"orientation":null},"sourceRefs":["music:source:lam2024"],"assertionLayer":"source-assertion","exceptions":["C fixed to huangzhong and chromatic pc indices are the paper convention, not established ancient Hz or twelve-tone equal-tempered tuning."],"evidence":{"sourceId":"music:source:lam2024","normalizedTextChars":[27988,28498],"text":"To narrow the analytical object to modes only, rather than any kind of note, I will replace the symbols pos note and pc note with pos final and pc final , which denote the modal final as the analytical object in the subscript. Labeling modes: weidiao / zhidiao 為調之調. [4.2] Historically, pentatonic modes have been represented both as ( pc pent , pos final ) or ( pc final , pos final ). (18) Consider these two modes: for D, E, G, A, C, the pc pent is C, the pc final is D, and the pos final is shang , for C, "}},{"id":"chinese-expanded:lam:mode:0:0","nativeName":"0 set 宮 final","aliases":[],"unit":"Lam-source-defined-mode-final-context","tradition":"Chinese","witnessId":"Lam2024","position":{"generation":null,"sequence":null,"cyclicCoordinate":null,"orientation":null},"sourceRefs":["music:source:lam2024"],"assertionLayer":"source-